{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_1","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc 'cat scratch/design-recovery/focus-review/council-drift-oct4/brief.md scratch/design-recovery/focus-review/council-drift-oct4/review-guidance/index.md'","aggregated_output":"# Council brief: how the deployed UI drifted from the design the owner liked, and what to render locally now (October 4, 2026, 16:45). Astra and Grok. Under 500 words each. Read-only.\n\n## What happened, in order (all files under /Users/farzanm4/Desktop/repos/oparax/scratch/design-recovery/focus-review/)\n1. Oct 2 to 4: the owner reviewed three accepted directions in the design lab (scratch/design-recovery/site, routes /v2/window, /v2/newsroom, /v2/deck) and 9 passes of a merged \"One\" (/v2/one). He rejected passes 1 to 7 on feel. Pass 8: \"Dex feed code looks good\" (Deck's feed code copied, only his verbatim asks applied). Pass 9: the sidebar became one bubble menu bottom left (his idea), Sources and Notifications pages added. Renders of pass 9: renders/{feed-open,onboarding-step-1..8,onboarding-done,login,setup,sources,notifications}.png; the originals: renders/{deck-feed,window-feed,newsroom-feed,window-building,deck-building}.png. Every note of his: PAGE-NOTES.md.\n2. Oct 4 night, owner: \"convert the real-life site code into the emerging one code... so that the actual site itself has the new UI rendered on it... Let the scratch folder remain.\" A council (council-convert-oct4/{astra,grok}.md) wrote a 10-step plan; two Opus builders executed steps 1 to 9 on main (commits d8596b7f to eed94e56); Vercel deployed to oparax.ai. The product's pages: app/login, app/signup, app/onboarding, app/[handle] (feed, building, ready), app/[handle]/sources, app/[handle]/notifications, components/monitor/bubble.tsx, components/auth/one-card.tsx, components/monitor/one-feed.tsx, lib/monitor/present.ts. The live database had 0 monitors; the builders could not sign in (hosted Supabase Auth, no test accounts). Renders of the product with its tiny fixture data: renders/product/{feed-clustered-dark,bubble-dark,login-dark,signup-dark,landing-dark}.png.\n3. Oct 4, 16:40, the owner, verbatim, after walking the live site signed in: \"Bro what the actual fuck is this, as far as I remembered I asked for my best liked UI to be sent to oparax.ai and this is horrible. Weren't we working through the three different styles along with the one style locally, and that's fine? Forget what's on oparax.ai right now. No need to change that, but why the fuck is the design so different from what I said, okay? It's just horrible. How is this possible? When my last thing was to send the one design that I like. Regardless, please can you render in the localhost browser first? I can see all of them. Please /council with Astra and Grok because I'm just lost on how this horrible thing went forward... whatever the consensus comes to, dispatch an Opus agent to just render my thing on localhost, or you do it, whatever. Do not focus on what's deployed right now in oparax.ai now.\"\nThe host did not see what he saw signed in (real feed with his real stories, the onboarding build, Sources, Notifications). The host is rebuilding the design lab and serving it on http://localhost:3000 again (all four styles) while you answer.\n\n## Questions\n1. Drift: compare the pass 9 renders with the product renders and the product code. Name, concretely, the 5 largest ways the deployed pages differ from what he accepted locally (data density, images, old blocks kept such as Daily Digests and Skipped, the old landing, no story fan, whatever else you find), and for each say whether it is a build mistake, a real-data gap (0 monitors, no images), or the plan itself.\n2. Process: where did the process break? Candidates: a design accepted on rich sample data was ported onto real data nobody could see; the conversion was a reinterpretation by builders instead of a port of the lab's components; the owner never accepted pass 9 on a render before it went to production; the host read \"send the one design I like\" as the One when he may mean one of the three originals. Pick the real causes, in order.\n3. Next action, one only: he wants \"my thing\" rendered on localhost so he can walk it. Say exactly what should be on localhost:3000 for his walk (the design lab's four styles as they are; or the One only; or the product app on fixture data) and what the host should ask him in at most 2 questions after he looks. Then the rule that prevents a repeat (for example: nothing deploys before he accepts the same page on localhost with real data).\n\nDeliver: RESULT: FINDINGS, then (1) numbered, at most 5 lines; (2) numbered causes, at most 4 lines; (3) the next action in 3 lines, the questions, the rule. No em dashes. Plain words; he reads this.\n# Selected review guidance\n\nUse only the skills relevant to the review. Read each full SKILL.md on demand from the linked directory. The review remains read-only. Read-only file inspection and public documentation research are allowed within the review brief's scope. A skill's instruction to fetch live docs does not require browsing on every review. Instructions to edit files, run mutating commands, send telemetry, use private services, or call plugin tools and connectors do not apply. The snapshot contains skill files only, with no runtime plugin access.\n\n## nextjs\n\nNext.js App Router architecture and implementation guidance.\n\nWhen to use: Review routing, Server Components, Server Actions, data fetching, caching, metadata, or deployment behavior.\n\nFull guidance: [SKILL.md](skills/nextjs/SKILL.md)\n\n## vercel-functions\n\nVercel function runtimes, streaming, and cron behavior.\n\nWhen to use: Review route handlers, background work, streaming, runtime limits, and scheduled jobs.\n\nFull guidance: [SKILL.md](skills/vercel-functions/SKILL.md)\n\n## routing-middleware\n\nVercel routing and middleware behavior.\n\nWhen to use: Review request routing, redirects, rewrites, and middleware boundaries.\n\nFull guidance: [SKILL.md](skills/routing-middleware/SKILL.md)\n\n## react-best-practices\n\nReact and TSX quality checklist for structure, hooks, accessibility, performance, and types.\n\nWhen to use: Review React components, hooks, client boundaries, rendering behavior, or TSX performance.\n\nFull guidance: [SKILL.md](skills/react-best-practices/SKILL.md)\n\n## shadcn\n\nOfficial shadcn component composition and project guidance.\n\nWhen to use: Review UI built with shadcn components, registries, presets, forms, or component composition.\n\nFull guidance: [SKILL.md](skills/shadcn/SKILL.md)\n\n## accessibility\n\nWCAG 2.2 accessibility guidance for web interfaces.\n\nWhen to use: Review semantics, keyboard use, focus, contrast, screen reader behavior, or accessibility acceptance criteria.\n\nFull guidance: [SKILL.md](skills/accessibility/SKILL.md)\n\n## ai-elements\n\nAI Elements guidance and local component references.\n\nWhen to use: Review a UI that depicts or controls an AI run, its steps, messages, or tool output.\n\nFull guidance: [SKILL.md](skills/ai-elements/SKILL.md)\n\n## reference-led-design\n\nThe owner's accepted design method: verbatim owner words, a screenshot board with his verdicts, acceptance criteria, distinct directions, image-anchored building.\n\nWhen to use: Propose or judge visual directions, explain what the owner responded to in reference screenshots, or extend an accepted design. Lanes use steps 1 to 4 read-only and cite board images.\n\nFull guidance: [SKILL.md](skills/reference-led-design/SKILL.md)\n\n## supabase\n\nSupabase guidance for Auth, SSR clients, RLS, and database changes.\n\nWhen to use: Review Supabase queries, Auth, RLS, migrations, client initialization, and ownership boundaries.\n\nFull guidance: [SKILL.md](skills/supabase/SKILL.md)\n\n## supabase-postgres-best-practices\n\nSupabase Postgres schema, SQL, RLS, and performance guidance.\n\nWhen to use: Review tables, indexes, policies, RPCs, queries, and migrations.\n\nFull guidance: [SKILL.md](skills/supabase-postgres-best-practices/SKILL.md)\n\n## ai-sdk\n\nVercel AI SDK generation, structured output, tool, and streaming guidance.\n\nWhen to use: Review model calls, output validation, tools, streaming, and provider integration.\n\nFull guidance: [SKILL.md](skills/ai-sdk/SKILL.md)\n\n## ai-gateway\n\nVercel AI Gateway routing, model, and cost guidance.\n\nWhen to use: Review Gateway model identifiers, routing, limits, usage, cost, and failure handling.\n\nFull guidance: [SKILL.md](skills/ai-gateway/SKILL.md)\n\n## typesafe-ai\n\nTypeSafe Jev judgment and typed answer guidance.\n\nWhen to use: Review Jev questions, scoring contracts, response validation, and judgment use.\n\nFull guidance: [SKILL.md](skills/typesafe-ai/SKILL.md)\n\n## prompt-format\n\nDraft assistant proposal for Oparax prompt and Jev question format; it is not an approved project rule.\n\nWhen to use: Consult when reviewing prompts, tool descriptions, untrusted data markers, or Jev questions. Treat its rules as nonbinding unless an approved plan or task explicitly adopts them.\n\nFull guidance: [SKILL.md](skills/prompt-format/SKILL.md)\n\n## instrument-integration\n\nPostHog client and server initialization guidance.\n\nWhen to use: Review analytics SDK setup, identity, capture configuration, and duplicate initialization.\n\nFull guidance: [SKILL.md](skills/instrument-integration/SKILL.md)\n\n## instrument-product-analytics\n\nPostHog product analytics guidance for meaningful user actions and identity.\n\nWhen to use: Review a feature or pull request for missing, duplicate, unsafe, or inconsistent product analytics.\n\nFull guidance: [SKILL.md](skills/instrument-product-analytics/SKILL.md)\n\n## instrument-error-tracking\n\nPostHog error tracking setup and capture guidance.\n\nWhen to use: Review server and client error capture, grouping, and sensitive data handling.\n\nFull guidance: [SKILL.md](skills/instrument-error-tracking/SKILL.md)\n\n## instrument-feature-flags\n\nPostHog feature flag instrumentation guidance.\n\nWhen to use: Review feature flag evaluation, rollout behavior, and analytics when flags are in scope.\n\nFull guidance: [SKILL.md](skills/instrument-feature-flags/SKILL.md)\n\n## instrument-llm-analytics\n\nPostHog AI observability guidance.\n\nWhen to use: Review model spans, token and cost capture, latency, and safe trace properties.\n\nFull guidance: [SKILL.md](skills/instrument-llm-analytics/SKILL.md)\n\n## stripe-best-practices\n\nStripe integration and subscription guidance.\n\nWhen to use: Review checkout, subscriptions, webhooks, idempotency, and key handling.\n\nFull guidance: [SKILL.md](skills/stripe-best-practices/SKILL.md)\n\n## stripe-docs\n\nStripe documentation lookup guidance.\n\nWhen to use: Review Stripe API assumptions against shipped guidance and official public docs.\n\nFull guidance: [SKILL.md](skills/stripe-docs/SKILL.md)\n\n## react-bits-pro\n\nLicensed React Bits Pro catalog, source integration, entitlement and harmonization guidance.\n\nWhen to use: Review React Bits Pro component or block choices and supplied source. Reviewers inspect files only; installation instructions do not grant install or MCP access.\n\nFull guidance: [SKILL.md](skills/react-bits-pro/SKILL.md)\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
